{"h":3106,"lines":[{"w":0.056390978495279964,"h":0.013241438119548032,"x":0.16541353321476604,"c":1,"t":"Test 3","y":0.087209302359345986},{"y":0.13122117885989248,"c":1,"w":0.28793607076009115,"x":0.16524051733746725,"h":0.017775694631562922,"t":"READING PASSAGE 2"},{"t":"You should spend about 20 minutes on Questions 14-26, which are based on Reading","c":1,"h":0.017497079877491051,"y":0.16709594350271917,"w":0.76691731770833338,"x":0.16541352158092573},{"t":"Passage 2 below.","c":1,"x":0.1635338368154893,"y":0.18604651134481087,"w":0.15789473215738933,"h":0.016142799711503786},{"w":0.015037593841552732,"t":"B","c":1,"y":0.4084302325218252,"h":0.013081395234588844,"x":0.16353383457761247},{"w":0.70864659627278648,"t":"How baby talk gives infant brains a boost","x":0.20112782957724507,"h":0.027688345138441761,"y":0.22086284555746261,"c":1},{"w":0.73319015502929696,"h":0.020069566912138348,"c":1,"y":0.26411621602368707,"x":0.20482965900931457,"t":"The typical way of talking to a baby - high-pitched, exaggerated and repetitious - is"},{"c":1,"t":"a source of fascination for linguists who hope to understand how 'baby talk' impacts","x":0.20672345568262235,"h":0.018802479475602207,"y":0.28173823360441153,"w":0.73129786173502609},{"h":0.01754387624019671,"c":1,"w":0.68233083089192703,"x":0.20676691527400504,"t":"on learning. Most babies start developing their hearing while still in the womb,","y":0.30087209289067007},{"w":0.70488723754882809,"t":"prompting some hopeful parents to play classical music to their pregnant bellies.","h":0.017487720604950074,"c":1,"x":0.20676690736308881,"y":0.31831395335455714},{"h":0.016108170218876006,"t":"Some research even suggests that infants are listening to adult speech as early","y":0.33708950446863872,"c":1,"x":0.20676692846909656,"w":0.69924809773763008},{"w":0.72376968383789064,"y":0.35315318385637839,"t":"as 10 weeks before being born, gathering the basic building blocks of their family's","h":0.019538998527060203,"c":1,"x":0.20672516580304906},{"c":1,"t":"native tongue.","w":0.12854068756103515,"x":0.20643325136591884,"y":0.37241729455024974,"h":0.016374344834955812},{"t":"Early language exposure seems to have benefits to the brain - for instance, studies","y":0.40695332165818121,"w":0.73129938761393232,"c":1,"h":0.019078935720194479,"x":0.20671597803886035},{"h":0.017463386864794206,"t":"suggest that babies raised in bilingual homes are better at learning how to mentally","x":0.2067669250275847,"w":0.72744359334309916,"y":0.42587209288591743,"c":1},{"c":1,"t":"prioritize information. So how does the sweet if sometimes absurd sound of infant-","x":0.2067669276471821,"w":0.71992477416992195,"h":0.016119401223108398,"y":0.44331395363126269},{"x":0.20676692702404201,"y":0.46072118472839318,"t":"directed speech influence a baby's development? Here are some recent studies","w":0.69924809773763019,"h":0.017476488986632455,"c":1},{"w":0.36842104593912756,"h":0.016097875080489432,"t":"that explore the science behind baby talk.","x":0.20488722129587728,"y":0.48100450710093501,"c":1},{"x":0.2048872280841412,"w":0.70864659627278648,"h":0.015988372635703296,"c":1,"y":0.51598837181952273,"t":"Fathers don't use baby talk as often or in the same ways as mothers - and that's"},{"t":"perfectly OK, according to a new study. Mark VanDam of Washington State","w":0.66917292277018237,"x":0.20488722180204338,"y":0.53343023239731036,"h":0.01744186072217524,"c":1},{"w":0.72932332356770835,"c":1,"h":0.015988372635703185,"t":"University at Spokane and colleagues equipped parents with recording devices and","y":0.55232558112172481,"x":0.20676690954106525},{"h":0.017483041275722089,"t":"speech-recognition software to study the way they interacted with their youngsters","c":1,"x":0.2048872114546621,"w":0.71992482503255206,"y":0.569767441728529},{"h":0.017441859494004786,"t":"during a normal day. 'We found that moms do exactly what you'd expect and what's","y":0.58720930259311388,"x":0.20676693051776188,"c":1,"w":0.72932327270507813},{"x":0.20488721031827614,"w":0.72932332356770835,"h":0.017456835189789799,"t":"been described many times over,' VanDam explains. 'But we found that dads aren't","y":0.60463618818546927,"c":1},{"t":"doing the same thing. Dads didn't raise their pitch or fundamental frequency when","h":0.016097875080489432,"x":0.20488722693480468,"c":1,"y":0.62491951035107929,"w":0.71804509480794287},{"w":0.73510818481445317,"h":0.020544254772139725,"t":"they talked to kids.' Their role may be rooted in what is called the bridge hypothesis,","y":0.64052730541602876,"c":1,"x":0.20481920542108545},{"c":1,"t":"which dates back to 1975. It suggests that fathers use less familial language to","w":0.68984959920247391,"x":0.20488723030615594,"h":0.017514862556727628,"y":0.6598837207971372},{"t":"provide their children with a bridge to the kind of speech they'll hear in public. 'The","y":0.67868641324835688,"w":0.71992482503255206,"h":0.016097875080489321,"x":0.20488721145414918,"c":1},{"y":0.6960721186921901,"w":0.70300750732421868,"t":"idea is that a kid gets to practice a certain kind of speech with mom and another","h":0.016137183902345087,"x":0.20300752444135819,"c":1},{"h":0.01918982722570417,"w":0.73131958007812492,"c":1,"x":0.20482691081802179,"y":0.71326686030117792,"t":"kind of speech with dad, so the kid then has a wider repertoire of kinds of speech to"},{"x":0.2048872191849436,"h":0.018895348808647294,"t":"practice,' says VanDam.","w":0.21428571065266924,"c":1,"y":0.73110465098811817},{"x":0.20294047084937308,"h":0.019238201173289782,"w":0.68622075398763027,"t":"Scientists from the University of Washington and the University of Connecticut","y":0.76691386216271251,"c":1},{"h":0.022458350973135421,"c":1,"t":"collected thousands of 30-second conversations between parents and their babies,","y":0.78138629679303062,"w":0.72955963134765622,"x":0.20479546367587584},{"x":0.20488721489146541,"w":0.69172932942708332,"h":0.016097875080489321,"c":1,"y":0.80521571166671091,"t":"fitting 26 children with audio-recording vests that captured language and sound"},{"x":0.20488720933572493,"y":0.82260141649633622,"h":0.016097875080489432,"t":"during a typical eight-hour day. The study found that the more baby talk parents","w":0.69548873901367192,"c":1},{"t":"used, the more their youngsters began to babble. And when researchers saw","x":0.20481813937026061,"y":0.83926182454654041,"w":0.6768171183268229,"h":0.01847790351469758,"c":1},{"t":"the same babies at age two, they found that frequent baby talk had dramatically","x":0.20300752998328098,"y":0.85898261456406289,"h":0.016097875080489432,"c":1,"w":0.6992480977376303},{"t":"boosted vocabulary, regardless of socioeconomic status. 'Those children who","w":0.67857142130533865,"y":0.87499999969705189,"h":0.017466194462330997,"x":0.2048872248548495,"c":1},{"t":"listened to a lot of baby talk were talking more than the babies that listened to more","x":0.20300751086204627,"y":0.89375402436188134,"w":0.72932332356770835,"h":0.017707662588538287,"c":1},{"w":0.024436089197794608,"h":0.014534883321060899,"t":"64","c":1,"x":0.15977443662290719,"y":0.96220930238016711}],"w":2400}